#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151883 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2b677c92-5390-5cd1-b1d3-b84d180c2b3e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Complex Conjugate of a Complex Vector"}] :question/id #uuid "203ff7a1-64cf-5564-8e7c-7ff9f652911a" :question/math-academy-id "e-6559" :question/problem "If ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041865/assets/518a42d25cd993f4bca2498bd9e91a466c7f0c4d71e109b6ab95c9717d34e9e0.png) find $\\,\\overline{\\mathbf{x}}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the complex conjugate of a vector, we take the complex conjugate of the entries of the vector. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\overset{―}{[\\begin{aligned}-2+5\\text{i} \\\\ 5-9\\text{i} \\\\ -7+8\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{-2+5\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{5-9\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{-7+8\\text{i}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2-5\\text{i} \\\\ 5+9\\text{i} \\\\ -7-8\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151884 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "689f9f44-4776-56a7-915f-d0dab0755002" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Components of the Real and Imaginary Parts of a Complex Vector"}] :question/id #uuid "a2c8f19f-6c69-5891-847e-b6ef26f657bf" :question/math-academy-id "e-6560" :question/problem "If ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041865/assets/19d1bb5ad60407748a9c624dee20931c3c70a4bbc3727c4172cfb40384ab6a72.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041865/assets/f7539ad7301462681681e738b905633b7aa73ca65b5512063e32fa22bcdc0d09.png) are the real and imaginary parts of the vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041865/assets/a7976c73a0aeb9f286a281c193b3a00b38e8bc0fa36a30e985fe1e8f80d7796b.png) what is the value of $ab+cd?$" :question/worked-solution "For the given vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041865/assets/4d6fc79d41790b29a966f7a3303329ab1b778856991ad5b3b85ee3965fce2e33.png) we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =[\\begin{aligned}-3+7\\text{i} \\\\ 5-2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(x)}+\\text{i}\\,{{[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore $a=-3, b=5, c=7$ and $d=-2,$ which implies that\n\n$$\nab+cd=(-3) \\cdot 5 + 7 \\cdot (-2) = -29.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151943 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3eaed693-68df-5da8-942d-408d6871358a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Real or Imaginary Part of a Scalar Given the Conjugate of a Scaled Vector"}] :question/id #uuid "5ec4fe6e-b357-5721-86d0-298df3fd33cf" :question/math-academy-id "e-7345" :question/problem "Find $\\textrm{Im}(k)$ given that \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041865/assets/c51689b9c3a6e7c0e16e5121c725d9400b377ceab8f955bba851c2686991365b.png)\nand\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041865/assets/1dbce6fee97471e3eb80d3ad5791f70311d6304f7a4d75fac77160e5ad9bee09.png)" :question/worked-solution "Since $\\overline{k\\mathbf{v}} = \\overline{k} \\, \\overline{\\mathbf{v}},$ we get the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{kv} & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,\\overset{―}{v} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}8\\text{i}-12 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,\\overset{―}{[\\begin{aligned}-4\\text{i} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}8\\text{i}-12 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,[\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{-4\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{0}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}8\\text{i}-12 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,[\\begin{aligned}4\\text{i} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}8\\text{i}-12 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4\\text{i}\\,\\overset{―}{k} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain that \n\n$$\n4\\textrm{i}\\,\\overline{k}  = 8\\textrm{i}-12\n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\\overline{k}=\\dfrac{8\\textrm{i}-12}{4\\textrm i} = 2+3\\textrm{i}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $k=\\overline{2+3\\textrm{i}}=2-3\\textrm{i}.$\n\nFinally, $\\textrm{Im}(k)=-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323949 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2b677c92-5390-5cd1-b1d3-b84d180c2b3e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Complex Conjugate of a Complex Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7c9d73a-9344-55b2-8dec-5a558f1ca005" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1+\\text{i} \\\\ -3+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323951} {:answer/id #uuid "5185efbb-fa85-55b9-937e-62dea56d475c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} \\\\ 4+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323952} {:answer/id #uuid "46e41095-97a0-5389-b0e3-115a081be1cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323953} {:answer/id #uuid "ff9d046b-4786-55b8-ab44-e625213a6219" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3-5\\text{i} \\\\ 3-\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323954} {:answer/id #uuid "62472621-f1dd-5617-8952-268885fb0c52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3+\\text{i} \\\\ 3+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323955}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62472621-f1dd-5617-8952-268885fb0c52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3+\\text{i} \\\\ 3+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323955} :answer-field/id #uuid "b69e2315-d99d-563d-b729-2e4cc71b7862" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323950}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "efa3ade7-3cc0-54f2-8c21-cc7467828f67" :question/math-academy-id "q-130888" :question/problem "Given the vectors\n${x}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2\\text{i} \\\\ -1-4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n${x}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1+3\\text{i} \\\\ -3-4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]$, then ${\\overset{―}{x}}_{1}+\\text{i}\\cdot {x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "To find the complex conjugate of a vector, we take the complex conjugate of the entries of the vector. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\overset{―}{x}}_{1} & =\\overset{―}{[\\begin{aligned}-2\\text{i} \\\\ -1-4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{-2\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{-1-4\\text{i}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\text{i} \\\\ -1+4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the second vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{i}\\cdot {x}_{2} & =\\text{i}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1+3\\text{i} \\\\ -3-4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\text{i}+3{\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\ -3\\text{i}-4{\\text{i}}^{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3-\\text{i} \\\\ 4-3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\overset{―}{x}}_{1}+\\text{i}\\cdot {x}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\text{i} \\\\ -1+4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3-\\text{i} \\\\ 4-3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3+\\text{i} \\\\ 3+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323956 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "689f9f44-4776-56a7-915f-d0dab0755002" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Components of the Real and Imaginary Parts of a Complex Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "227fbdd9-7905-5980-9652-94d6b482e967" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\,\\text{Re}(v)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],$ $\\,\\text{Im}(v)=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\,$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323958} {:answer/id #uuid "6c866e9e-044f-5db7-9f2d-c1a4d06cbfe6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\,\\text{Re}(v)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],$ $\\,\\text{Im}(v)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\,$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323959} {:answer/id #uuid "772ae916-003c-5ba8-8fa2-6dfe26f58559" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\,\\text{Re}(v)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ $\\,\\text{Im}(v)=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\,$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323960} {:answer/id #uuid "06be2c48-9e06-5f9b-8ed9-bc5941f9b434" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\,\\text{Re}(v)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],$ $\\,\\text{Im}(v)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\,$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323961} {:answer/id #uuid "ab367af1-dc80-51f3-8124-7ca419577c11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\,\\text{Re}(v)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],$ $\\,\\text{Im}(v)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\,$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323962}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab367af1-dc80-51f3-8124-7ca419577c11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\,\\text{Re}(v)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],$ $\\,\\text{Im}(v)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\,$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323962} :answer-field/id #uuid "4cd32239-ddba-5647-958f-301705492605" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323957}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "17864892-57d7-55ae-aad6-9fa186f9a721" :question/math-academy-id "q-130891" :question/problem "Find the real and imaginary parts of the vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}\\text{i}+2 \\\\ 4-2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "For the given vector $\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}2\\text{i}-1 \\\\ -\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =[\\begin{aligned}\\text{i}+2 \\\\ 4-2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2+\\text{i} \\\\ 4-2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(v)}+\\text{i}\\,{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(v)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323963 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3eaed693-68df-5da8-942d-408d6871358a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Real or Imaginary Part of a Scalar Given the Conjugate of a Scaled Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a48050f4-91ad-5d08-8b56-bff5e769d8c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323965} {:answer/id #uuid "3f995f06-2886-51c5-8b9e-c30b48b4d81b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323966} {:answer/id #uuid "7bc4f20f-a7d4-5a88-9e81-ebeb1010d6ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323967} {:answer/id #uuid "a9976bdc-ebac-51b2-9cf7-bf42027ee299" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323968} {:answer/id #uuid "e69c8bcd-2fad-58b8-b682-8ab26abf8eaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323969}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7bc4f20f-a7d4-5a88-9e81-ebeb1010d6ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323967} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7989046-68a5-5696-941f-dd27b0836109" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323964}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ac819df9-c6d9-5a9a-b344-5d1c936bc2fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-130893" :question/problem "Find $\\text{Re}(k)$ given that\n$v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$\\overset{―}{kv}=[\\begin{aligned}18-18\\text{i} \\\\ 6-30\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Since $\\overset{―}{kv}=\\overset{―}{v},$ we get the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{kv} & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,\\overset{―}{v} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}18-18\\text{i} \\\\ 6-30\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,\\overset{―}{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}18-18\\text{i} \\\\ 6-30\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,[\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{3} \\\\ \\overset{―}{3+2\\text{i}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}18-18\\text{i} \\\\ 6-30\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3-2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}18-18\\text{i} \\\\ 6-30\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3\\overset{―}{k} \\\\ (3-2\\text{i})\\overset{―}{k}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3\\overset{―}{k}=18-18\\text{i} \\\\ (3-2\\text{i})\\overset{―}{k}=6-30\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{k}=6-6\\text{i}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we obtain the true statement\n\n$$\n(3-2\\text{i})(6-6\\text{i})=6-30\\text{i}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=\\overset{―}{6-6\\text{i}}=6+6\\text{i}.$\n\nFinally, $\\text{Re}(k)=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323970 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3eaed693-68df-5da8-942d-408d6871358a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Real or Imaginary Part of a Scalar Given the Conjugate of a Scaled Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0ca16cc-a1de-51ab-9634-ebce60d2e6b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323972} {:answer/id #uuid "28bd076f-0625-5b80-ab0a-437a83339ff6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323973} {:answer/id #uuid "4a806def-a6f9-5438-889c-444cc519b01f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323974} {:answer/id #uuid "4c472f45-4815-5427-ba1f-d20ee4856748" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323975} {:answer/id #uuid "f09e9b58-9de6-5320-89b8-a58bfdb47824" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323976}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0ca16cc-a1de-51ab-9634-ebce60d2e6b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323972} :answer-field/id #uuid "e742b114-6117-55eb-9b3c-8211bdb1474e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323971}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "240d967e-b792-5dc9-9e88-43ab9a9df5cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-130894" :question/problem "Find $\\text{Re}(k)$ given that\n$v=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -5-\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$\\overset{―}{kv}=[\\begin{aligned}-20+28\\text{i} \\\\ 18-40\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Since $\\overset{―}{kv}=\\overset{―}{v},$ we get the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{kv} & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,\\overset{―}{v} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-20+28\\text{i} \\\\ 18-40\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,\\overset{―}{[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -5-\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-20+28\\text{i} \\\\ 18-40\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,[\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{4} \\\\ \\overset{―}{-5-\\text{i}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-20+28\\text{i} \\\\ 18-40\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -5+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-20+28\\text{i} \\\\ 18-40\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4\\overset{―}{k} \\\\ (-5+\\text{i})\\overset{―}{k}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4\\overset{―}{k}=-20+28\\text{i} \\\\ (-5+\\text{i})\\overset{―}{k}=18-40\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{k}=-5+7\\text{i}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we obtain the true statement\n\n$$\n(-5+\\text{i})(-5+7\\text{i})=18-40\\text{i}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=\\overset{―}{-5+7\\text{i}}=-5-7\\text{i}.$\n\nFinally, $\\text{Re}(k)=-5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323977 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3eaed693-68df-5da8-942d-408d6871358a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Real or Imaginary Part of a Scalar Given the Conjugate of a Scaled Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2326a24d-2afb-5aa6-aefa-252d646f45a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323979} {:answer/id #uuid "d70a987d-b696-582b-8168-41aa0ded3723" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323980} {:answer/id #uuid "59050ad0-fbeb-50d5-b81b-c1339f36905f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323981} {:answer/id #uuid "ec6aa73c-1ba6-54e4-8512-af22cab39c4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323982} {:answer/id #uuid "330ea075-87da-5fd6-af52-72f9bd16ca3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323983}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d70a987d-b696-582b-8168-41aa0ded3723" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323980} :answer-field/id #uuid "fbba9145-405d-58f6-b3ba-4e02c3930e44" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323978}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5b5fdbad-bcf8-53ee-9213-59f31a714452" :question/math-academy-id "q-130898" :question/problem "Find $\\text{Im}(k)$ given that \n$v=[\\begin{aligned}-2\\text{i} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$\\overset{―}{kv}=[\\begin{aligned}-6+8\\text{i} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Since $\\overset{―}{kv}=\\overset{―}{k}\\,\\overset{―}{v},$ we get the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{kv} & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,\\overset{―}{v} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-6+8\\text{i} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,\\overset{―}{[\\begin{aligned}-2\\text{i} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-6+8\\text{i} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,[\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{-2\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{0}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-6+8\\text{i} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,[\\begin{aligned}2\\text{i} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-6+8\\text{i} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\text{i}\\,\\overset{―}{k} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain that \n\n$$\n2\\text{i}\\,\\overset{―}{k}=-6+8\\text{i}\\,⟹\\,\\overset{―}{k}=\\frac{-6+8\\text{i}}{2\\text{i}}=4+3\\text{i}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $k=\\overset{―}{4+3\\text{i}}=4-3\\text{i}.$\n\nFinally, $\\text{Im}(k)=-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152512 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2b677c92-5390-5cd1-b1d3-b84d180c2b3e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Complex Conjugate of a Complex Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0096aee-63a3-53d9-b8f6-938dab3e5144" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 - 2\\textrm{i} \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149983} {:answer/id #uuid "cf679583-8655-57c3-bc2d-f29969749c4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 + \\textrm{i} \\\\ -1 + \\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149984} {:answer/id #uuid "f073731d-3f8c-56b8-828a-760e537a7136" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 + \\textrm{i} \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149985} {:answer/id #uuid "0c8e57f2-aeed-5930-ac48-bdb02fe02d07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 5 + \\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149986} {:answer/id #uuid "2902eac7-8a38-5d4f-af18-1d963e1345e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 + \\textrm{i} \\\\ -1 + 4\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149987}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f073731d-3f8c-56b8-828a-760e537a7136" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 + \\textrm{i} \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149985} :answer-field/id #uuid "08a28b38-d7d5-52d7-ad19-54f9d0948250" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149982}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b0d06576-e31f-5746-8662-1003ad31dfe2" :question/math-academy-id "q-38387" :question/problem "Given the vectors ${x}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1+\\text{i} \\\\ 2+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]$ and ${x}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2-4\\text{i} \\\\ 2+3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]$, then ${\\overset{―}{x}}_{1}+\\text{i}\\cdot {x}_{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "To find the complex conjugate of a vector, we take the complex conjugate of the entries of the vector. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\overset{―}{x}}_{1} & =\\overset{―}{[\\begin{aligned}1+\\text{i} \\\\ 2+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{1+\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{2+2\\text{i}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} \\\\ 2-2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the second vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{i}\\cdot {x}_{2} & =\\text{i}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2-4\\text{i} \\\\ 2+3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\text{i}-4{\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\ 2\\text{i}+3{\\text{i}}^{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4+2\\text{i} \\\\ -3+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\overset{―}{x}}_{1}+\\text{i}\\cdot {x}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} \\\\ 2-2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4+2\\text{i} \\\\ -3+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5+\\text{i} \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152513 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "689f9f44-4776-56a7-915f-d0dab0755002" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Components of the Real and Imaginary Parts of a Complex Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85a3c80b-5c62-5b72-a020-2d845dd23b9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149989} {:answer/id #uuid "b0fb2aa3-cca1-5b23-85ed-2128d04bf457" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149990} {:answer/id #uuid "f4d084d5-bdb4-5b61-a57b-990cfd2d5975" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149991} {:answer/id #uuid "0748f060-151a-5440-a50d-dcca5de48481" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149992} {:answer/id #uuid "79332dc6-84ea-5c0d-9b75-af572f440a9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149993}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79332dc6-84ea-5c0d-9b75-af572f440a9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149993} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca13a5fc-9db1-59c8-99e1-fa63aa1fe673" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149988}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0f76aac6-fb1f-5af4-a2f0-ac47a47590be" :question/math-academy-id "q-38388" :question/problem "If $\\,\\text{Re}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,\\text{Im}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ d\\end{aligned}]\\,$ are the real and imaginary parts of the vector $\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2+4\\text{i} \\\\ 5-2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$ then what is the value of $ad+bc?$" :question/worked-solution "For the given vector $\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2+4\\text{i} \\\\ 5-2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =[\\begin{aligned}2+4\\text{i} \\\\ 5-2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(x)}+\\text{i}{{[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore $\\,a=2,b=5,c=4$ and $d=-2$, which implies that \n\n$$\nad+bc=2\\cdot (-2)+5\\cdot 4=16.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323984 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2b677c92-5390-5cd1-b1d3-b84d180c2b3e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Complex Conjugate of a Complex Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b1ccfe2-5149-5296-910c-5891c834dd3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-9+6\\text{i} \\\\ -9+3\\text{i} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323986} {:answer/id #uuid "d271ec7b-25d5-5634-bff1-4522194bc878" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6+9\\text{i} \\\\ 3+9\\text{i} \\\\ -3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323987} {:answer/id #uuid "5abca682-36e