{x}=$" :question/worked-solution "To find the complex conjugate of a vector, we take the complex conjugate of the entries of the vector. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\overset{―}{[\\begin{aligned}4+3\\text{i} \\\\ 2-2\\text{i} \\\\ 5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{4+3\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{2-2\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{5\\text{i}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4-3\\text{i} \\\\ 2+2\\text{i} \\\\ -5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323998 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "689f9f44-4776-56a7-915f-d0dab0755002" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Components of the Real and Imaginary Parts of a Complex Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b3cf990-3e54-5fe8-9e7d-fed5cca84706" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324000} {:answer/id #uuid "77818183-e3c6-5440-a4e6-c5210a12f74c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "44" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324001} {:answer/id #uuid "5c067d15-66b1-513d-ae6c-d499406de67f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "76" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324002} {:answer/id #uuid "2bbd1fab-9777-51d4-a1ae-f7f642779b20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324003} {:answer/id #uuid "03c3a5ed-2b6e-578e-b20e-745c554357b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324004}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b3cf990-3e54-5fe8-9e7d-fed5cca84706" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324000} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e7b760a-0db1-5aa0-89ec-047df9e9d754" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323999}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5143b7be-56af-519f-aeef-652c6062a8fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-76049" :question/problem "If $\\,\\text{Re}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,\\text{Im}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ d\\end{aligned}]\\,$ are the real and imaginary parts of the vector $\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-4+9\\text{i} \\\\ 1+8\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$ then what is the value of $bc-ad?$" :question/worked-solution "For the given vector $\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-4+9\\text{i} \\\\ 1+8\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =[\\begin{aligned}-4+9\\text{i} \\\\ 1+8\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(x)}+\\text{i}\\,{{[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore $\\,a=-4,b=1,c=9$ and $d=8$, which implies that \n\n$$\nbc-ad=1\\cdot 9-(-4)\\cdot 8=41.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186324005 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "689f9f44-4776-56a7-915f-d0dab0755002" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Components of the Real and Imaginary Parts of a Complex Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "769fa1f0-18ef-5745-b581-b6c5ef87f96e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "43" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324007} {:answer/id #uuid "5dccf669-8a3a-5558-868e-2b40664de9af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324008} {:answer/id #uuid "6053698d-8243-519a-8f3c-d808e1ca53bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324009} {:answer/id #uuid "b036cad6-7fa9-5e8c-a60e-655163058e53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324010} {:answer/id #uuid "ac8100ae-84c5-5cb6-a6be-7ee1211f533a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324011}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "769fa1f0-1